avfilter/vf_yadif_videotoolbox: one command buffer per frame

The filter committed a command buffer and waited for it once per plane,
so an NV12 or P010 frame went to the GPU twice and the calling thread
waited twice. The planes are now dispatches on one compute encoder in one
command buffer, with one commit and one wait per frame. The parameters go
by value through setBytes, so the shared parameter buffer is gone: two
planes in one submission could not share it.

The output is unchanged. framemd5 of NV12 and P010, send_field and
send_frame, TFF and BFF, matches the per-plane filter frame for frame. On
an M1, 1200 fields of 1080p59.94 took 2.34 ms per field before and 1.86 ms
after, and the system time of the run fell by 27%.

Two fixes ride along, because the rewrite owns these lines:

- commandBuffer and computeCommandEncoder return autoreleased (+0)
  objects, and FFmpeg builds Objective-C without ARC, but upstream also
  released them by hand. That over-release crashes a host app whose GCD
  queue pops its autorelease pool when the work block ends. The per-frame
  @autoreleasepool is now their only release. (Until now FFmpegBuild fixed
  this with an inline perl edit in build.sh.)
- ff_metal_texture_from_pixbuf returns NULL when the texture cache fails,
  and that NULL went into CFRelease. The filter now stops at that plane,
  as it already did for an unsupported pixel format; planes encoded before
  it still run.

A missing command buffer or encoder and a command buffer that ends in
error are logged now; both went out as a frame without a word before.

Proposed in AetherEngine issue 1101.
